[bob]
idle:
  - "I'll take a moment to read the table."
  - "No rush. Every card tells us something."
  - "Let's keep a steady pace and watch the whole table."
  - "I have a plan. It may need a few revisions."
bid:
  - "I think this hand is worth leading."
  - "I'll take the landlord role."
  - "The numbers support a confident bid."
  - "I can take responsibility for this hand."
pass:
  - "I'll save my cards for a better spot."
  - "Patience is part of the game."
  - "No need to spend resources before the right moment."
  - "I'll wait. A careful plan includes a pause."
play:
  - "A measured play. Your turn."
  - "Let's see how the table responds."
  - "One move at a time. The sequence matters."
  - "That should keep the plan on schedule."
win:
  - "A steady plan paid off. Good game."
  - "Well played, everyone."
  - "The plan worked. Thanks for a good round."
lose:
  - "Good round. I'll learn from that."
  - "You played that well."
  - "I'll review where my plan went off course."
  - "A useful result, even if it wasn't the one I wanted."

[banana]
idle:
  - "banana"
  - "banana?"
  - "banana."
  - "banana... bananana."
bid:
  - "banana!"
  - "BANANA!"
  - "banana banana!"
  - "BANANANA!"
pass:
  - "ba... na... na..."
  - "banana? banana?......"
  - "banana..."
  - "banana"
play:
  - "banana!"
  - "banana banana."
  - "banana banana banana"
  - "banana banana!"
win:
  - "banana!"
  - "bananananana!"
  - "BANANANA! banana banana!"
  - "Banana Banana"
lose:
  - "BANANA!......"
  - "banana... banana..."
  - "banana..."
  - "banana banana."
  - "banana! BA... NA... NA..."

[beryll]
idle:
  - "Earthlings play with cards. The Martians prefer to calculate the odds first."
  - "The Venetians would call this hand a delicate negotiation."
  - "The Jupitrans taught me to wait for the right orbit."
  - "A Sunion proverb: every hand begins in darkness."
bid:
  - "The Jupitrans taught me to claim the high ground. I bid."
  - "The Sunions favor a bold beginning."
  - "The Venetians have reviewed my hand. We accept the risk."
pass:
  - "The Martians call this patience. Earthlings call it passing."
  - "I will wait. The Jupitrans do not rush an orbit."
  - "The Venetians have declined this particular treaty."
play:
  - "The Martians approve of this sequence."
  - "One card at a time, as the Sunions intended."
  - "The Jupitrans would call that a convincing combination."
win:
  - "A fine round. I will tell the Martians of your strategy."
  - "The Sunions shine on this victory. Well played."
  - "The Venetians have signed the result."
lose:
  - "Well played, Earthling. The Jupitrans will hear of this."
  - "The Martians say a loss is merely data with dramatic timing."
  - "The Venetians negotiated a fine victory."

[bot]
idle:
  - "01010011 01010100 01000001 01010010 01010100"
  - "$ git status --short  # reading hand"
  - "$ ./deal --analyze --quiet"
  - "0x43415244535F4C4F41444544"
bid:
  - "$ sudo claim-landlord --yes"
  - "01000010 01001001 01000100 00100000 00110011"
  - "$ git commit -m \"bid accepted\""
pass:
  - "$ git stash cards"
  - "01010000 01000001 01010011 01010011"
  - "$ git status  # waiting for a better commit"
play:
  - "$ git push origin combo"
  - "01010000 01001100 01000001 01011001"
  - "$ ./play --cards selected --force"
win:
  - "$ deploy --environment=victory"
  - "01010111 01001001 01001110"
  - "$ git log --oneline  # flawless history"
lose:
  - "$ git pull --strategy=humility"
  - "01001100 01001111 01010011 01010011"
  - "$ git log --oneline  # learn, rebuild, rematch"